# Line endings are LF, everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF
# and git prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every add. Worse than the noise
# is what it hides: a file can then report as modified while its content is
# byte-identical to HEAD, so `git status` shows changes that do not exist and
# `git pull` refuses over them. That cost a real debugging detour.
#
# Everything here is text and nothing is a Windows-only script, so LF is correct
# on every platform. Editors on Windows have handled LF for two decades.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the things where it matters most.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
